s://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egg_as_food"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Muscle","chain":["Complete protein and choline","Muscle repair and growth","More muscle, better physique"],"effect":"indirect","text":"Eggs and yolks are a staple of bodybuilding and appearance diets as a cheap, complete protein with fat and choline, supporting muscle gain. The protein feeds muscle repair and growth when paired with training and enough calories. Egg protein quality is well documented."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Whole eggs and egg yolks are a common food in bodybuilding and general nutrition, and are discussed in appearance-focused communities mainly as sources of protein, fat and choline. A hard-boiled chicken egg provides roughly 12.6 g of protein and 294 mg of choline per 100 g, and egg protein scores the maximum on the PDCAAS protein-quality scale.[1]","Debate about eggs has centred on dietary cholesterol (about 373 mg per 100 g). Meta-analyses published in the 2010s and 2020s reached differing conclusions, with several finding no association between moderate egg intake and cardiovascular risk in the general population.[1] Wikipedia notes that raw eggs carry a salmonella risk and that cooked egg protein is more bioavailable than raw.[1]"],"infobox":[["Type","Whole food (animal-derived)"],["Protein","About 12.6 g per 100 g, hard-boiled[1]"],["Choline","About 294 mg per 100 g[1]"],["Cholesterol","About 373 mg per 100 g[1]"]],"sections":[{"h":"Nutrition","paras":["Per 100 g, a hard-boiled chicken egg contains about 155 kcal, 10.6 g fat and 1.12 g carbohydrate, along with vitamin B12, riboflavin, vitamin D, vitamin A, phosphorus and choline.[1] The yolk holds most of the fat and the choline, while the white is mostly water and protein.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Cholesterol and health research","paras":["Studies of egg intake and heart disease have been inconsistent. A 2013 meta-analysis found no link to heart disease or stroke, while another that year reported modestly higher risk, and a 2018 review of randomized trials found eggs raised LDL and HDL cholesterol compared with no eggs, though not compared with low-egg diets.[1] Two 2020 meta-analyses and an umbrella review found no association between moderate intake and cardiovascular risk in the general population.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Food safety","paras":["Salmonella can contaminate eggs; a USDA study cited by Wikipedia estimated about 1 in 30,000 US eggs was affected, and cooking to 71 C kills the bacteria.[1] Raw egg protein is about 51 percent bioavailable versus about 91 percent for cooked.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found on egg yolk for appearance outcomes such as skin or hair. General research on eggs concerns cardiovascular risk, diabetes and nutrition, as described above.[1]"],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Egg as food - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egg_as_food","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[{"title":"Egg as food - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egg_as_food","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"eggs are lowkey shit source of protein","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/eggs-are-lowkey-shit-source-of-protein.1417194/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250426082002/https://looksmax.org/threads/eggs-are-lowkey-shit-source-of-protein.1417194/"},{"title":"Eggs mog so hard","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/eggs-mog-so-hard.1386669/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250403031843/https://looksmax.org/threads/eggs-mog-so-hard.1386669/"},{"title":"I can’t make eggs taste good","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/i-cant-make-eggs-taste-good.1790305/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251228190835/https://looksmax.org/threads/i-cant-make-eggs-taste-good.1790305/"},{"title":"raw eggs question","url":"https://looksmax.org/thre